    "description": "Class III, mains or battery-operated, self-indicating, non-automatic weighing instruments designated SW Series, comprising the ED, ER PLUS, ER PLUS-M, SW-1, ER JR and PW-II models and their variants. Plastic construction, operator's keypad, stainless steel load receptor, level indicator, operator and customer display. Devices: initial zero setting device, semi-automatic zero setting device, zero tracking device, zero indicator, net indicator, semi-automatic subtractive tare balancing device, gravity compensation, check weighing and weighing unstable samples modes (SW-1S, SW-1C, SW-1W, SW-1LR, SW-1WR, ER JR, PW-II and ED models only), processing of non-weighed items, price computation (weighed and non-weighed items), totalisation (when connected to a printer), Price Clear and Tare Clear functions, 3-point calibration. Sealing: access to load cell and calibration switch prevented by wire-and-seal or tamper-evident sticker on the enclosure. Software designated V2.xx.x or V3.xx.x, displayed at power up; download via RS232 port requires access to main board (jumper JP1)."
